Package: vyro-compositor
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Vyro display server (Path B) packaged for Ubuntu (experimental)
 vyro-compositor is the from-scratch DRM/KMS display server developed in
 the Vyro OS Path B Linux+userland track. It owns /dev/dri/card0 directly,
 speaks the Vyro IPC protocol over /run/vyro/compositor.sock, and renders
 the glassmorphism window chrome itself with no Wayland or X11 layer.
 .
 This package is the Path A (Ubuntu remix) repackaging that lets users
 pick "Vyro Compositor (experimental)" at the GDM login screen alongside
 the default GNOME session.
